@startuml usecase
title COLORS Web Application - Use Case Diagram
left to right direction
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam actorStyle awesome

actor "Registered User" as User
database "MySQL Database\n(COP4331)" as DB <<system>>

rectangle "COLORS Web Application" {
  usecase "Log In" as UC_Login
  usecase "Hash Password (MD5)" as UC_Hash
  usecase "Validate Session\n(read cookie)" as UC_Session
  usecase "Add Color" as UC_Add
  usecase "Search Colors" as UC_Search
  usecase "Log Out" as UC_Logout
  usecase "Display Error Message" as UC_Error
}

User --> UC_Login
User --> UC_Add
User --> UC_Search
User --> UC_Logout

UC_Login ..> UC_Hash : <<include>>
UC_Add ..> UC_Session : <<include>>
UC_Search ..> UC_Session : <<include>>
UC_Error .> UC_Login : <<extend>>\n[invalid credentials]
UC_Error .> UC_Add : <<extend>>\n[DB error]

UC_Login --> DB
UC_Add --> DB
UC_Search --> DB

note right of UC_Login
  Users are pre-created in the database;
  the app has no registration use case.
end note
@enduml
